1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:04,359
Okay so if loneliness is a gap between the connection you need and the connection you have.
好了，如果孤独是你需要的联系和你已经拥有的联系之间的差距，

2
00:00:04,359 --> 00:00:08,840
The question becomes what do you actually do with that gap what do you do with that information.
那么问题就变成：面对这个差距，你到底做些什么？知道这些之后，又能做些什么？

3
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:17,799
Because most advice is like take yourself on a date light a candle practice self care do a face mask and like fine but that's not addressing the actual feeling.
因为大多数建议都是自己约会、点蜡烛、照顾自己、敷面膜。这些当然可以，但没有回应那种真实的感受。

4
00:00:17,799 --> 00:00:21,720
Here's what I've been thinking about instead treat loneliness like a signal not a verdict.
我最近换了个想法：把孤独当成一个信号，而不是对自己的判决。

5
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:27,944
There's this idea in psychology that loneliness functions like hunger or thirst it's your body telling you that you need something it's information.
她提到一种心理学观点：孤独像饥饿或口渴一样运作，是身体在告诉你需要些什么，它提供的是信息。

6
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:31,550
And your instinct is usually to just make it go away as fast as possible.
而你的本能通常是让它尽快消失。

7
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:35,960
Scroll instagram text your ex situationship fill that silence with random podcasts.
刷 Instagram，给前任或暧昧对象发消息，或者随便放些播客来填满安静的时间。

8
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:40,030
But what if you just listen to it first what is this feeling actually telling me that I need.
但如果先听听它呢？这种感受究竟在告诉我，我需要什么？

9
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,359
Do I need deeper connections with the people I already have.
我需要与现有的人建立更深的联系吗？

10
00:00:42,359 --> 00:00:48,280
Do I need to put myself in more social situations do I need to just be alone less the feeling itself has information.
我需要更多参与社交场合吗？还是需要少一些独处？感受本身就含有信息。

11
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:55,390
Second stop optimizing for never feeling lonely I think we've been sold this idea that if you're doing life correctly you should never feel lonely.
第二点，别再追求永远不孤独。她觉得大家被灌输了一个想法：只要日子过对了，就不应该感到孤独。

12
00:00:55,400 --> 00:01:00,200
You should have enough friends enough plans enough inner peace that loneliness doesn't touch you.
你应该有足够多的朋友、足够多的安排，以及足够的内心平静，让孤独碰不到你。

13
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:06,440
But that's just that real everyone feels lonely sometimes even people with tons of friends even people in relationships.
但她接着否定了这种期待：每个人有时都会孤独，包括朋友很多的人，也包括有伴侣的人。

14
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:13,000
The problem isn't the feeling it's that we made it mean something bad about us we made it mean that we failed in some way.
问题不是这种感受本身，而是我们让它意味着自己不好，意味着自己在某方面失败了。

15
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,400
The goal isn't to never feel lonely it's to stop adding the shame on top of it when you do.
目标不是永远不孤独，而是在孤独时，不再额外给它加上一层羞耻感。

16
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:22,359
To stop thinking something fundamentally broken about you because you feel a completely normal human emotion.
别因为自己体验了一种完全正常的人类情绪，就认为自身有根本性的问题。

17
00:01:22,359 --> 00:01:29,880
Remember that you're not going to be alone forever this specific chapter of your life where you have solitude so much quiet this much space to figure out who you are.
记住，作者认为你不会一直独处。人生的这个阶段，有这么多安静和空间，让你弄清自己是谁。

18
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:39,880
Without constantly adapting someone else it's temporary at some point you're going to have a partner or kids or a job that just consumes all your time or aging parents who need you.
不必不断适应别人，这个阶段也是暂时的。她设想以后你也许会有伴侣、孩子、占满时间的工作，或需要你的年迈父母。

19
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:45,000
And you'll look back on this time and think I had so much space back then and I wish I used it differently.
你可能会回头想：那时我有那么多空间，要是当时换种方式利用它就好了。

20
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,069
Do the things that you actually want to do learn that weird hobby take the trip become the person who just does things without waiting for someone to do it with them.
去做真正想做的事，学那个有点怪的爱好，去旅行，成为不用等别人陪着就去做事的人。

21
00:01:51,079 --> 00:01:57,560
Because this time doesn't last and you can spend it either waiting for it to be over or you can spend it building life that you don't want to just escape from.
因为这段时间不会永远持续。你可以一直等着它结束，也可以用它建立一种自己不想逃离的生活。

22
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:00,359
Good morning everyone it is the next day and today is saturday.
大家早上好，已经是第二天了，今天星期六。

23
00:02:00,359 --> 00:02:04,750
We're going on a hike this hike was not my idea I don't think it will ever be my idea to go on a hike.
我们要去远足。这不是我提议的，我想自己大概永远也不会主动提议去远足。

24
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:08,280
But my friends want to go on a hike I haven't seen them in a while so I'm excited to see them.
但我的朋友们想去远足。我有一阵子没见他们了，所以很期待见面。

25
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:14,120
We're going to go an hour outside of new York do a 3 hour hike come back get food maybe even sauna.
我们要去纽约城外约一小时的地方，走三个小时，再回来吃饭，也许还会去蒸个桑拿。

26
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:19,079
I feel like for the amount of times I've woken up in the middle of the night I feel surprisingly well rested today.
虽然夜里醒了很多次，今天的精神却出乎意料地好。

27
00:02:19,079 --> 00:02:25,560
I woke up at like 1 00 I woke up at 6 00 I just got up at like 7 00 made breakfast did some miscellaneous errands again.
我大概一点醒过，六点也醒过，七点左右就起床了，做了早餐，又处理了一些杂事。

28
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:31,160
Also I've just spent this morning watching culinary class wars literally so good such such good cinema guys.
还有，我今天早上一直在看 Culinary Class Wars，真的很好看，太精彩了。

29
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:39,079
Alone time as identity formation something else I've been thinking about is how being alone actually shapes who you are especially if you're someone who's always just been around other people.
“独处与身份形成”。我还在想，独处怎样塑造我们，尤其是对那些一直待在人群里的人。

30
00:02:39,079 --> 00:02:45,160
If you're always in relationships always in group chats always adjusting yourself to match the room you don't really get to hear your own voice.
如果总在恋爱中、总待在群聊里，总是调整自己以适应周围的人，你就很难听见自己的声音。

31
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:49,240
You get very good at reacting at mirroring at becoming whoever makes sense in that moment.
你会很擅长回应、模仿别人，变成当时那个场合里最合适的样子。

32
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:55,879
But you don't always develop clear tastes strong preferences or opinions that aren't influenced by just the last person you talk to.
但你不一定能形成清晰的品味、鲜明的偏好，或不受刚刚交谈的那个人影响的观点。

33
00:02:55,879 --> 00:03:02,200
Being alone forces you to confront questions like what do I actually like when no one's around what do I think not just what I agree with.
独处迫使你面对一些问题：没人时我究竟喜欢什么？我自己怎么想，而不只是赞同什么？

34
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:05,879
What food do I want to get on a random tuesday afternoon what kind of life feels right to me.
一个普通周二的下午，我想吃什么？什么样的生活对我来说才合适？

35
00:03:05,879 --> 00:03:11,400
And that can be uncomfortable especially if you never had to answer those questions before but that discomfort is kind of the point.
如果你从没回答过这些问题，可能会不舒服。但那份不舒服，某种程度上正是重点所在。

36
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:18,119
I think a lot of people who hate being alone don't actually hate solitude they hate the sudden absence of external feedback.
我觉得许多讨厌独处的人，其实不是讨厌安静独处，而是讨厌外界反馈突然消失。

37
00:03:18,119 --> 00:03:25,400
Because when you're alone there's no one to tell you who you are so remember being alone isn't the absence of people it's the presence of yourself.
因为独处时没人告诉你你是谁。所以记住，独处不是人的缺席，而是你自己的在场。

38
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:28,280
When you're used to being around others being alone feels like deprivation.
当你习惯和别人在一起时，独处就像被剥夺了什么。

39
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:32,680
Like you're missing out on the real experience which is happening wherever other people are and you just have a lot of fomo.
你觉得自己错过了真正的体验，而那些体验正在别人那里发生，于是充满错失的焦虑。

40
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:38,439
But the shift is realizing that you're not waiting for life to happen you're not in the waiting room this is it.
但转变在于意识到：你不是在等待生活发生，也不是坐在等候室里。这就是生活本身。

41
00:03:38,439 --> 00:03:41,480
The time you spend alone is still your life it still counts.
你独处的时间仍然是你的人生，仍然有意义。

42
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:46,150
And you can either treat it like dead time until the next social thing or you can treat it like actually living.
你可以把它当成下一次社交前的空白时间，也可以把它当成真正在生活。
